pentadsolver-gpu — authors and provenance
==========================================

GPU optimisation kernels (steps 4–11), runtime kernel dispatch, benchmarking
campaign, MPI enablement, problem-size scale-up study, FP32 accuracy study,
and the ADI-structured (shared-coefficient) solver:
    Sidhant Kumar Agrawal  <sidhantkragrawal@gmail.com>
    CS908 MSc dissertation, University of Warwick
    Supervisor: Dr Gihan Mudalige

Original CPU and CUDA pentadiagonal solver base (library structure, CPU
OpenMP/AVX2 solver, MPI reduced-system solver, ADI cavity application,
correctness suite):
    Nidhi Shukla
    CS907, University of Warwick

The overall design follows the Oxford scalar tridiagonal solver "tridsolver":
    Endre László, Mike Giles, Gihan Mudalige, and contributors
    https://github.com/OP-DSL/tridsolver   (BSD 3-Clause, OP-DSL)

Build scaffolding uses cpp-best-practices/project_options (fetched at configure
time). Tests use Catch2; micro-benchmarks use Google Benchmark.
